						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">we went on mad early on saturday (1pm or so) on the yeti stage... it was my first time at the gorge and the beauty of our surroundings just took my breath away... it felt great being backstage like 20 deep... it was like we brought a whole neighborhood, the way it should be.&nbsp; the set ended up being my favorite show we&#039;ve ever put on... better then the release party... we had the full band... amos miller on keys, mark oi on guitar, aaron walker-loud on drums, camilo estrada on bass, and wd4d on cuts... and helping out on vocals was jerm from alpha-p (do u), sistahailstorm &amp; ispire from canary sing (warriors rrreeemix), kwame (no label), and rufio (rest o&#039; me dayz)... as well as nin-g the hyphogropher dancing along with hailstorm, rufio, etc... if you missed it, damn ya&#039;ll missed a show!!!&nbsp; ozomatli killed it as well... i&#039;m sad we missed bjork... but the land and the sky definitley outshined everyone (it was so beautiful)&nbsp; to everyone that came throo... thanks!&nbsp; we&#039;re in phoenix now... hella homesick and i can&#039;t wait to see ya&#039;ll mothertruckers again...<br /><br />southendfalife<br />-- teodros</td>
